# 1. THE IMAGE THAT LOADED — crates/bootloader/src/main.rs, fn main (the #[entry]),
#    the KELF image-identity witness. The flight log MUST show:
#      KELF min=0x0 max=0x34b748 pg=<n>
#    A different max = a different kernel. This is FLIGHT.md §C.1 and it is scored FIRST.

# 2. THE MEDIUM IT LOADED FROM — crates/bootloader/src/main.rs, fn read_boot_volume_serial,
#    printed at the log::info! four lines below the KELF line. The flight log MUST show:
#      boot volume FAT serial 0xde001a13 (extended BPB BS_VolID)
#    A different serial = the board booted a DIFFERENT PHYSICAL MEDIUM than this write.

# 3. THE MEDIUM MOUNTED AT / — arch/aarch64/sdmmc_tegra.rs, fn root_probe (RPS witness).
#    ⚠ THIS IS A SECOND, PHYSICALLY DIFFERENT CARD: the Orin's NATIVE SD slot, which
#    sdmmc_root_bind binds to /, /boot AND /apps. THIS SCRIPT DOES NOT WRITE IT.
#    The flight log will show:
#      [sdmmc] root mount source=tegra-sd card_blocks=<n> -> OK label="<L>" vol_id=0x<V>
#    REQUIRED BEFORE SCORING ANY FILESYSTEM QUESTION: <L> must be "UNAOS-ORIN".
#    On render9 it read label="UNAOS-PI" vol_id=0xabfbdefa — a stale Pi card — while the
#    boot volume serial was 0xde001a13. TWO MEDIA. Nothing in the kernel compares them
#    (see PROGRESS.md §5: drivers/block.rs::set_boot_volume_serial is x86_64-only), so
#    THE COMPARISON IS THE SCORER'S JOB UNTIL THAT cfg IS WIDENED.
#    ⚠ render11 onward (BOOTROOT, exec-orin22-bootroot): the [sdmmc] root family is DELETED.
#    Its ABSENCE is expected; the root witness is instead
#      [vfs] root = boot volume serial=0xde001a13 source=<usb|global|tegra-sd> ... ::
#    and any other UnaOS disk mounts at /volumes/<LABEL>. Score with scorer11.sh.
